A poor loving wife sells her beautiful hair to buy her husband a watch chain, only to learn he sold his watch to buy her combs, turning useless gifts into proof of the wisest love.

1. Poor Christmas Eve Longing  (passages 1-1)
    Della has almost no money but desperately wants a fine Christmas gift worthy of Jim.
       -> Having almost nothing yet wanting something worthy pushes her to look at what they
       still own of value.
2. Two Treasures And Resolve  (passages 2-2)
    The couple own only two prized things, her long hair and his heirloom watch, before she
    rushes out determined to act.
       -> Knowing their only treasures are hair and watch sets up her decision to give up one to
       honor the other.
3. Hair Sold For Chain  (passages 3-3)
    Della sells her hair to buy a quiet platinum chain for his watch and hurries home to fix her
    shorn looks.
       -> Giving up her hair to get the chain leaves her anxious about how Jim will see her
       changed looks.
4. Anxious Return And Reassurance  (passages 4-5)
    Della fears Jim will find her less pretty after his shocked stare, but he insists his love
    is unchanged before giving her a package that brings joy then tears.
       -> His reassurance and mysterious gift leave the joy turned to tears unexplained until
       its contents and cost are revealed.
5. Useless Gifts Wisest Love  (passages 6-6)
    Jim reveals he sold his watch to buy combs for hair Della no longer has, and their foolish
    sacrifices are called the wisest giving of all.
